data.content:
## Migration: `EventProcessor` → .NET 8

### Pattern Classification

| Usage | Pattern | Replacement |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| `while (true)` loop | Cancellable work loop | `CancellationToken` checked in loop |
| `ManualResetEvent.WaitOne()` | Blocking call interruption | `WaitHandle.WaitAny` with `token.WaitHandle` |
| `Thread.Interrupt()` | Wake blocked thread | Cancellation signal wakes `WaitAny` |
| `Thread.Abort()` | Forcible termination | `CancellationTokenSource.Cancel()` — cooperative |

---

### Migrated Code

```csharp
public class EventProcessor : IDisposable
{
    private readonly ManualResetEvent _newEvent = new(false);
    private readonly Queue<string> _queue = new();
    private readonly CancellationTokenSource _cts = new();
    private Thread? _thread;
    private readonly object _lock = new();

    public void Start()
    {
        _thread = new Thread(RunLoop);
        _thread.Start();
    }

    private void RunLoop()
    {
        var token = _cts.Token;
        var waitHandles = new[] { _newEvent, token.WaitHandle };

        while (!token.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            // Blocks until either a new event arrives OR cancellation is requested
            int index = WaitHandle.WaitAny(waitHandles);

            if (index == 1) // token.WaitHandle was signaled → stop
                break;

            _newEvent.Reset();

            string? item = null;
            lock (_lock)
            {
                if (_queue.Count > 0)
                    item = _queue.Dequeue();
            }

            if (item is not null)
                Handle(item);
        }
    }

    public void Enqueue(string item)
    {
        lock (_lock) { _queue.Enqueue(item); }
        _newEvent.Set();
    }

    public void Stop()
    {
        _cts.Cancel();          // signals token.WaitHandle, waking RunLoop
        _thread?.Join(5000);    // wait up to 5s for graceful exit
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        Stop();
        _cts.Dispose();
        _newEvent.Dispose();
    }

    private void Handle(string item) { /* ... */ }
}
```

---

### Key Changes Explained

1. **`Thread.Abort()` / `Thread.Interrupt()` → `CancellationTokenSource.Cancel()`**  
   Cancelling the token signals `token.WaitHandle`, which unblocks `WaitAny` immediately — no forced exception injection needed.

2. **`WaitOne()` → `WaitHandle.WaitAny(event, token.WaitHandle)`**  
   This is the critical change. The thread now wakes for *either* new work or a cancellation request.

3. **`while (true)` → `while (!token.IsCancellationRequested)`**  
   Cooperative exit — the loop terminates voluntarily.

4. **Added `IDisposable`**  
   `CancellationTokenSource` leaks timers/callbacks if not disposed.

---

### Pitfalls to Watch

| Pitfall | Why it matters |
|---------|---------------|
| **Race: multiple items enqueued before `WaitAny` returns** | The original code had this bug too — `Reset()` could clear the signal before draining all items. Consider draining the full queue in a loop after waking. |
| **Not disposing `CancellationTokenSource`** | Causes timer/callback leaks. Always `Dispose()`. |
| **Assuming cancellation is instant** | If `Handle(item)` is long-running, `Stop()` blocks until it finishes. Pass `token` into `Handle` if it does I/O or heavy work. |
| **`Thread.Interrupt` is also obsolete** | .NET 9 marks it `SYSLIB0046`. Don't substitute one for the other. |
| **Removing the 5s timeout safety net** | The old code used `Abort()` as a fallback. With cooperative cancellation there is no forcible kill — ensure `Handle()` respects cancellation or accept the delay. |

---

### Bonus: Drain-all-items fix (recommended)

The original had a subtle bug where multiple enqueues could be lost. Drain the queue fully on wake:

```csharp
_newEvent.Reset();

List<string> items;
lock (_lock)
{
    items = new List<string>(_queue);
    _queue.Clear();
}

foreach (var item in items)
{
    if (token.IsCancellationRequested) break;
    Handle(item);
}
```

This also adds a cancellation checkpoint between items for faster shutdown.
